/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>NAGAYAMA K. ET AL.: 'Direct Hydrogenation of Carboxylic Acids to Corresponding Aldehydes Catalyzed by Palladium Complexes in the Presence of Pivalic Anhydride' CHEM. LETT. no. 11, 1998, pages 1143 - 1144, XP002925572</text><sources><source category="XP" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1108706A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>JAPAN SCIENCE &amp; TECH CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAYAMA KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO AKIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAYAMA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, AKIO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAYAMA KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO AKIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAYAMA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, AKIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process which makes it possible to prepare aldehydes under mild reaction conditions with a high efficiency through the reduction of carboxylic acids with molecular hydrogen. Specifically, a process of reducing an organic carboxylic acid with molecular hydrogen in the presence of a catalyst into an aldehyde corresponding to the acid, characterized by conducting the reduction in the presence of a dehydrating agent such as a carboxylic anhydride.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un procédé permettant de préparer des aldéhydes dans des conditions de réaction douces, à des rendements élevés, par la réduction d'acides carboxyliques avec l'hydrogène moléculaire. L'invention porte notamment sur un procédé de réduction d'un acide carboxylique organique avec l'hydrogène moléculaire en présence d'un catalyseur en un aldéhyde correspondant à l'acide, ce procédé consistant à effectuer la réduction en présence d'un agent de déshydratation tel que l'anhydride carboxylique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>